font="3" color="432D14" direction="1" style="0">RETURN</LABEL><NOTE_TEXT a="7,4" b="233,16.6" font="4" color="432D14" style="4" fill="0" direction="3" border_style="0">Q14 · Solar-cell optical investigation plan</NOTE_TEXT><NOTE_TEXT a="147,21" b="233,148" font="1" color="432D14" style="5" fill="2" direction="3" border_style="0">## Solar-cell optical investigation plan

**Post-16 · ages 16–19**

Annotate the circuit, test conditions and data-recording points for changes in distance, angle and illumination. The spatial/optical arrangement remains a separate apparatus sketch; TinyCAD does not calculate it from a schematic.

### Your investigation

Record a prediction, follow the stated task and compare the result with your prediction.

### This activity

Annotate the circuit, test conditions and data-recording points for changes in distance, angle and illumination. The spatial/optical arrangement remains a separate apparatus sketch; TinyCAD does not calculate it from a schematic.

### Getting started

This is a connection-planning drawing. Follow each labelled net, identify the real terminals and add your bench measurements. No simulation is attached.



**Explain:** Use an equation, a truth table or a state sequence to justify your prediction. Include units and discuss the model assumptions.

Check the physical layout with your teacher before construction.</NOTE_TEXT></TinyCAD><DSNSETTINGS><SHOW_RULERS>1</SHOW_RULERS></DSNSETTINGS><NETLIST_TYPES><TYPE name="default"/></NETLIST_TYPES></TinyCADSheets>